    "lead": "Picture Jen, a career coach who's had a \"free guide\" sitting on her site for a year. Forty pages! Nice cover. Hardly anybody signs up, and the few who do never book a call. Ouch. If she came to us, we'd say the problem probably isn't her writing. A lead magnet tends to earn emails when it makes one narrow promise, can be read in a single sitting, and ends with one next step. We'd put that same promise on her opt-in page, on the PDF cover and in the first email, send the file by email, and then judge the whole thing by opt-ins and clicks on that next step. That's really it. Below we walk through how we'd build it, from the very first sentence to launch day, plus the numbers that show whether it's pulling its weight.",
