    "lead": "Say Ray spent thirty years as a firefighter in Ohio and finally wants his stories in a memoir. His daughter suggests a ghostwriter. Ray frowns. \"Isn't that... cheating? Is it even legal?\" Good news, Ray. Ghostwriting is legal in the US. Hiring someone to write your memoir, business book or ebook and publishing it under your name is generally lawful, and a signed contract settles who owns the copyright and how the writer gets paid. Trouble starts when ghostwritten work is used to deceive, like schoolwork handed in for a grade or a book that invents credentials. So where are those lines? How's ghostwriting different from plagiarism, what should the contract include and how does credit work? Here's general information on all of it.",
