          "They're not, though. In a ghostwriting deal, both people sign off on the secrecy in writing. Nobody in the room is being fooled! Plagiarism is a whole other act. And those academic integrity rules? They're about schoolwork turned in for a grade. Ray's memoir, published and sold in bookstores, lives outside them."
