          "So picture Ray reading his draft contract at the kitchen table. What's he hoping to find? What the book is, how long, who it's for and when it's due. The fee and when he pays it, ideally fixed for that scope. How many revision rounds, and how he approves the outline and chapters. An NDA he signs before handing over a single photo or note. A written copyright assignment to him, signed before anyone writes. Whether the writer gets named, thanked or left off. A promise that the text is original. How AI tools get used, and what he'll be told about them. And what happens to the pages and the money if things stop early.",
          "Our [ghostwriter contract checklist](/blog/ghostwriter-contract-checklist-nda-and-rights) goes clause by clause, and our guide to [whether a ghostwriter owns your book](/blog/does-a-ghostwriter-own-your-book-rights) digs into the copyright side. This is general information, so ask an attorney how these rules apply to your own contract."
