    "lead": "Picture Marcy, a retired nurse (we made her up for this post), who just uploaded her first Kindle guide and is staring at two little radio buttons on the pricing screen. 35% or 70%? It looks like a trick question. It isn't, mostly. On Amazon.com the 70% option pays 70% of the list price minus a delivery cost of $0.15 per MB, and only for ebooks priced from $2.99 to $12.99. The 35% option pays 35% of the list price and charges no delivery cost at all. Paperbacks run on their own formula. Kindle Unlimited pays out of a monthly fund. We'll walk Marcy through all of it with real numbers, using Amazon's KDP help pages as of October 2026.",
