    "lead": "Short answer? Roughly 4 to 8 months if you're self-publishing with professional help, 6 to 18 months if you're writing it yourself, and 2 to 4 years if you go the traditional publishing route. Why so long? Because \"write and publish\" is secretly four projects stacked end to end: writing, editing, production and release. Most timeline advice only talks about the first one. That's how a \"three-month book\" ends up launching fifteen months later. It happens all the time. Below we go phase by phase, show you where the calendar really vanishes (hint, it's mostly waiting around and redoing things, very little of it is typing), and finish with three sample schedules you can hold up against your own deadline.",
    "cta": "Get a dated book schedule",
